    {
      "type": "p",
      "label": "Repository contributions",
      "text": "Awesome Copilot documents a collection of agents, instructions, skills and plugins. Anthropic Skills explicitly distinguishes open-source examples from source-available document skills."
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "label": "Choose a contribution",
      "items": [
        "Read one relevant procedure and its pinned sources rather than installing a whole collection.",
        "Keep a generic workflow separate from an optional tool and host formatting.",
        "Record actual versions, capabilities, paths and commands before use.",
        "Retain original evidence, blocked sources, unrun checks and unresolved choices.",
        "A documented capability, user report, local observation and proposed Atlas practice are different kinds of evidence."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "label": "Coverage limits",
      "text": "This is a curated reference set. It is not a popularity ranking, a compatibility certification or proof that the procedures improve every task. Laya, AgentRC and autonomous experiment patterns need a task-specific comparison. Library and gist reuse terms are recorded per inspected source. No repository is activated by reading this page."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "label": "Gap review: workflow use and checks",
      "text": "Use the repository directory when comparing feasible approaches, then plan a bounded trial of the selected workflow and its checks before adoption. A stage connection is a reading recommendation. It does not install a repository, establish comparative superiority or turn a directory entry into a verified project integration."
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "label": "Gap review: acceptance outputs",
      "items": [
        "A shortlist records the specific job, candidate revision, reviewed contribution, license constraints and reason for considering each option.",
        "The trial plan links the relevant Atlas procedure and defines expected artifacts, representative inputs and acceptance checks.",
        "The adoption decision records actual trial evidence or states not run, with conditional and experimental qualifications retained."
      ]
    }
  ],
